-- Round 006 (2026-08-22) — adversarial-review repair actuals vs the expectations
-- pre-registered in round-006-pre.rofl. All six review findings were severity:
-- minor; five acted on, one WONT-FIX with reason. Assert-only, never retract.
-- Evidence artifacts:
--   run_id: rofl-conformance-1787361952086 (post-repair harness run)
--   post-repair conformance-report.json sha256 =
--     4c2701458e868fce81a804f54ef4e8e58aeca7a43e83c6dec774452ee1b0d832 —
--     BYTE-IDENTICAL to the archived round-005 report
--     (rounds/round-005.report.json, same sha), so no separate archive is kept.

-- ── Repairs (recorded as repairs, not re-litigated hypotheses) ──

-- F1 REPAIRED: catalog.rs test base_relations_registered_with_executor_arities
-- now reads each base relation's arity LIVE from builtin::registry() and the
-- name set from plan::BASE_RELATIONS — the arity lock is mechanical like the
-- name drift guard, no literal (name, arity) pair list remains.
repair[a](exp_p1_catalog_consistent_zero_plan_change, arity_lock_now_mechanical_against_builtin_registry).

-- F2 REGISTERED as deliberate call C6 (no code change; canonical BYTES encode
-- arity explicitly, so identity is unaffected):
-- C6: an arity-0 Term renders as the BARE functor (`quiescent`, no parens) on
--     the as_str / wire text surface, deviating from the contract's uniform
--     `functor(a1,…,an)` canonical-text shape. Deliberate (Prolog/atom
--     convention; `f()` is noise for atoms), pinned by
--     datalog::tests::term_accessors_are_deliberate. P2+'s fid/state-sha TEXT
--     surfaces (if any are built on as_str rather than canon bytes) inherit
--     this convention and must consult this registration first.
repair[a](exp_p1_gate_complete, arity0_term_bare_functor_rendering_registered_as_c6).

-- F3 REPAIRED: declare() identity now spans EVERY declared field —
-- arity/strategy/cardinality/temporal/semiring/key_cols/reverse/author_priority
-- (excluded: assigned id, runtime-mutable stats). A same-logical-shape
-- redeclare differing in a physical axis is E-CAT-001, never a silent drop
-- (P3 dispatch and tag_fold key off semiring/key_cols). Per-axis tests added in
-- conflicting_redeclaration_is_e_cat_001_identical_is_idempotent. No P1 caller
-- can trip the tightened check: declare_default is name-level get-or-declare
-- (early return), with_base_relations declares fresh names only.
repair[a](exp_p1_catalog_consistent_zero_plan_change, e_cat_001_extended_to_all_declared_fields).

-- F4 WONT-FIX (registered, out of scope): storage_v2::multi_shard::tests::
-- test_commit_batch_performance_scaling is a pre-existing flaky wall-clock
-- assertion (failed once under parallel load in the review's first run, green
-- in isolation and in every full run since). The file is untouched by P1
-- (`git diff --name-only | grep multi_shard` empty); a robustness fix
-- (medians / wider bound / serialization) is a separate task for the owner —
-- governance forbids drive-by changes outside phase scope.
repair[a](exp_p1_gate_complete, flaky_perf_test_wontfix_preexisting_out_of_scope_flagged_to_owner).

-- F5 REPAIRED: new test derive::canon::tests::
-- multi_byte_varint_lengths_order_by_encoding_bytes_not_numeric_length pins the
-- multi-byte LEB128 branch of the §9.2 order on BOTH length-prefixed variants:
-- Str lengths 300 vs 200 and BigInt 300- vs 200-byte minimal magnitudes each
-- assert Ord ≡ canon-bytes lex AND the documented inversion
-- (varint(300)=[AC 02] < varint(200)=[C8 01] byte-lex → longer payload sorts
-- FIRST); equal-length case falls through to content bytes.
repair[a](exp_p1_canon_order_laws_green, leb128_multibyte_branch_pinned_by_targeted_test).

-- F6 REPAIRED at commit time: round-005-pre.rofl is committed in its OWN commit
-- ahead of the implementation commit on rofl-v1, making the pre-registration
-- ordering git-auditable (this file is written before those commits exist; the
-- commit shas live in git, not here — the ledger never guesses).
repair[a](exp_p1_gate_complete, round_005_pre_git_anchored_in_own_commit_before_implementation).

